Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::the_partition_checks_are_total_on_one_entry`.

The defect: the partition check tests only the start of a used entry against the usable range,
so an entry that starts inside the range and ends past its last block is accepted, and a
partition written there would overwrite the backup entry array.

Expected to fail: the assertion that an accepted used entry ends at or before the last usable
block.
diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/table.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/table.rs
--- a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/table.rs
+++ b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/table.rs
@@ -596,7 +596,6 @@
             return Err(Error::PartitionRange { index: i });
         }
         if e.first_logical_block_address < header.first_usable_logical_block_address
-            || e.last_logical_block_address > header.last_usable_logical_block_address
         {
             return Err(Error::PartitionOutsideUsable { index: i });
         }
